<title>UK: Fannie Mae prices $500 mln 10-year bond.</title>
<headline>Fannie Mae prices $500 mln 10-year bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal National Mortgage Association's $500 million 10-year callable global bond has been priced, joint lead managers Goldman Sachs International and Lehman Brothers said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The deal was launched on Tuesday.</p>
<p>+ + +</p>
<p> AMT	  $500 MLN  COUPON     7.93	MATURITY   *20.SEP.06</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE  99.945    PAY DATE    20.SEP.96</p>
<p> FULL FEES  0.325     REOFFER    99.945    SPREAD	+98 BP</p>
<p> MOODY	AAA	 LISTING    LUX	 PAY FREQ    SEMI-ANN</p>
<p> S&amp;P	  =	   DENOMS (K) 10	  SALE LIMITS =</p>
<p> NEG PLG    NO	  CRS DEFLT  NO	  FORCE MAJ   YES</p>
<p> MGT/UND    0.075     SELL CONC  0.25	PRAECIPUUM  NONE</p>
<p> UNDERLYING GOVT BOND 7.00 PCT U.S. T-NOTE DUE 15.JUL.06</p>
<p> NOTES     *CALLABLE AT PAR AFTER THREE YEARS.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
</text>
